Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the official tools structure. Let me create a detailed report of my findings.

## Official Tools Pattern & Structure - Comprehensive Analysis

Based on my thorough exploration of the official tools in `packages/tools/official/`, here's the complete guide for creating new official tool packages:

---

### 1. DIRECTORY & FILE STRUCTURE

Every official tool follows this standardized structure:

```
packages/tools/official/{tool-name}/
├── package.json          # Package metadata with tpmjs config
├── tsconfig.json         # TypeScript configuration
├── tsup.config.ts        # Build configuration
├── src/
│   └── index.ts         # Main implementation file
└── dist/                # Built output (generated)
```

**Key Pattern**: Single-source-of-truth approach - all tool code goes in `src/index.ts`, which is compiled to ESM by tsup.

---

### 2. PACKAGE.JSON STRUCTURE

All official tools follow this template:

```json
{
  "name": "@tpmjs/tools-{tool-name}",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "description": "...",
  "type": "module",
  "keywords": ["tpmjs", "{category}", "...", "agent"],

  "exports": {
    ".": {
      "types": "./dist/index.d.ts",
      "default": "./dist/index.js"
    }
  },

  "files": ["dist"],

  "scripts": {
    "build": "tsup",
    "dev": "tsup --watch",
    "type-check": "tsc --noEmit --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile tsconfig.tsbuildinfo",
    "clean": "rm -rf dist .turbo"
  },

  "devDependencies": {
    "@tpmjs/tsconfig": "workspace:*",
    "tsup": "^8.5.1",
    "typescript": "^5.9.3"
  },

  "dependencies": {
    "ai": "6.0.49"
  },

  "publishConfig": { "access": "public" },
  "repository": {
    "type": "git",
    "url": "https://github.com/tpmjs/tpmjs.git",
    "directory": "packages/tools/official/{tool-name}"
  },
  "homepage": "https://tpmjs.com",
  "license": "MIT",

  "tpmjs": {
    "category": "ops|data|sandbox|agent|...",
    "frameworks": ["vercel-ai"],
    "env": [
      {
        "name": "ENV_VAR_NAME",
        "description": "...",
        "required": true,
        "default": "optional-default-value"
      }
    ],
    "tools": [
      {
        "name": "toolFunctionName",
        "description": "...",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "paramName",
            "type": "string|number|object|...",
            "description": "...",
            "required": true
          }
        ],
        "returns": {
          "type": "ReturnTypeName",
          "description": "..."
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Critical Notes**:
- All dependencies should be from `ai: 6.0.49` for tool definitions
- External API libraries (like `@e2b/code-interpreter`) go in dependencies
- `tpmjs` metadata section is required for integration discovery
- For multi-tool packages, list ALL exported tools in the `tools` array

---

### 3. TSCONFIG.JSON

Standard and identical across all tools:

```json
{
  "extends": "@tpmjs/tsconfig/base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "outDir": "dist",
    "rootDir": "src"
  },
  "include": ["src"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
```

---

### 4. TSUP.CONFIG.TS

Identical across all tools (ESM with type definitions):

```typescript
import { defineConfig } from 'tsup';

export default defineConfig({
  entry: ['src/index.ts'],
  format: ['esm'],
  dts: true,
  clean: true,
  treeshake: true,
  splitting: false,
});
```

---

### 5. SRC/INDEX.TS IMPLEMENTATION PATTERNS

#### 5.1 IMPORTS
Always start with:
```typescript
import { jsonSchema, tool } from 'ai';
```

#### 5.2 SINGLE-TOOL PACKAGES (e.g., base64-encode, sprites-exec)

**Pattern**:
```typescript
// Define input and output types
interface ToolInput {
